# Copy this file to `.env` in the repo root and fill in your key:
#     cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is gitignored; never commit a real key.
#
# Only needed for the scripts that call an LLM:
#     Scripts/run_pipeline.py    (generate assessments)
#     Scripts/run_eval.py        (LLM-judge scoring)
#     Scripts/run_guideline.py   (strategy generation from the Art. 10 guide)
# Every analysis, plotting and scraping script runs without it.
#
# All models are called through OpenRouter (https://openrouter.ai) with the `openai` client.
# Create a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys and add credit. The runs in this repo used
# openai/gpt-5.4, openai/gpt-5.5, anthropic/claude-opus-4.7, deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro
# and mistralai/mistral-medium-3-5.
#
# Model IDs and reasoning effort are constants at the top of each script (MODEL,
# REASONING_EFFORT), not environment variables. `run_pipeline.py` also accepts
# --model / --effort / --api-key. A key already exported in your shell takes precedence
# over this file (python-dotenv does not override existing variables).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your-openrouter-api-key-here
